WEBVTT

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.480
It's the fairyland at the bottom of the universe.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:41.000
Dreams in a wasteland.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.930
A town overrun with violence.

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.260
The idiot's utopia.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.730
The planet people call "Endless Illusion."

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:55.600
A man named Van, who operates the strongest Armor.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:59.110
A girl named Wendy...

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:01.050
who's searching for her kidnapped brother.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.820
Though they walk together...

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:07.420
there seems to be a great distance between them.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:10.820
Will the day come when it is shortened by even a little bit?

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.150
And the Rain Kept Falling

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.790
I'm sorry! It was my fault!

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.790
Listen!

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.220
Forgive me! Please! I'm begging you!

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.220
Come on. Please.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:51.450
So, is everything cool?

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:54.230
Sorry about that.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.140
Van!

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:05.740
Are you all right?

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:07.580
Why wouldn't I be?

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.850
You look like you're in pain!

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.910
I'm fine.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:16.760
But don't get mixed up with strange people.

00:03:17.790 --> 00:03:19.230
It causes problems.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.550
But...

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:25.190
Damn it. Which way is the river?

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.140
You shouldn't be cooling yourself off if you're not feeling well.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.160
Get out of here.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.770
You should get some sleep.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:39.210
Not while I'm looking!

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.910
Hey, you. I told you to go.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.010
My name is Wendy!

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.020
You could at least remember my name.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.190
What?

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.660
Why are you being so careless?

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:56.630
What?

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.090
Van?

00:03:58.770 --> 00:03:59.670
Van!

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.590
Hey, can you hear me?

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:03.670
Hey!

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.700
Wake up, Van!

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.670
You'll go over the falls if you don't get up!

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.280
It's cold!

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:31.290
You're heavy.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.010
Don't touch.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.320
But you have a terrible fever.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.410
I know. Leave me alone.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.610
Leave you alone?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.430
Like I said, give me a little quiet...

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.320
Van?

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:21.040
I'm sorry, Yukiko.

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:10.980
You're covered in sweat.

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.390
You've still got a fever, don't you?

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.880
A wound? No...

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:47.090
Are you conscious? Keep still. I'm wiping you off now.

00:07:47.630 --> 00:07:48.560
Go home.

00:07:49.730 --> 00:07:51.320
If you stay with me...

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.520
Go back...

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:57.060
to your town.

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:09.840
I can't do that.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:13.690
Elena.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:16.950
Elena.

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.620
I'll be back soon. Keep an eye on him?

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:13.780
It can't be.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:13.940
Come back Wendy.

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:16.480
Wendy, where did you go?

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:17.250
- Come quick. Let's play together.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:18.950
- Wendy!
- Come quick. Let's play together.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:19.250
- Come quick. Let's play together.

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:21.220
Wendy...

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:29.120
Right.

00:10:31.560 --> 00:10:35.660
What am I doing? I must seem like such a fool.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:52.080
Where's...

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:55.270
where's your master?

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:04.190
Damn it.

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:10.930
I haven't ridden it in a while. That must be why.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:46.890
I can't even get the place right?

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:49.430
So long.

00:12:10.090 --> 00:12:11.130
That's right!

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.060
Horace was making rug rats again.

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:15.090
He's sure got a lot of free time.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.460
Excuse me.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:30.310
Where can I find a doctor?

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.370
Excuse me!

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:32.850
I'd like those, please.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:40.190
Go straight along the road and you'll come to a hospital.

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:42.480
Thank you very much.

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:48.800
Hey, she's carrying a gun on her back.

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.860
I don't understand these strangers at all.

00:12:51.170 --> 00:12:53.200
Dr. Collins in the Internal Medicine Department please report to Division 2.

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:54.900
I want the doctor to come see him.
Dr. Collins in the Internal Medicine Department please report to Division 2.

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:55.930
Please!

00:12:58.870 --> 00:13:01.540
The doctor only visits people who live in town.

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:03.240
But he's sick!

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:07.750
It's a rule. A lot of strange things go on outside of town.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:09.740
I'd appreciate it if you stop bothering me.

00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:12.050
What am I going to do?

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.420
Hey, is someone sick?

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:16.150
A person I know has a fever.

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.090
The facilities aren't as nice as here...

00:13:19.090 --> 00:13:21.120
but the place where I work is also a hospital.

00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:34.980
So, were you able to borrow the equipment?

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:38.440
Yes. It was a lot of trouble, but you should have it by next week.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:43.410
Of course we should. He was my apprentice to begin with.

00:13:44.020 --> 00:13:44.950
So?

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.650
What is the patient's condition?

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.920
Well, um...

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:52.390
You can relax!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.590
Dr. Denehee is a renowned physician.

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:57.030
Although his face is a little scary.

00:13:57.030 --> 00:13:58.090
Hey.

00:13:58.430 --> 00:13:59.730
Sorry.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:05.000
The only thing I can't cure is my own body.

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.870
Come on, talk to me.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:10.900
Yes.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.280
Armor rider?

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:20.210
Yes. But he hasn't ridden at all recently.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:24.480
I wish the Armor riders would all smash each other to pieces.

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:28.000
We've got some Armor riders in this town too.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:31.270
They're stupid, violent, and have no regard for human life.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.290
Van's different!

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:37.590
He's stupid and violent, but he doesn't disregard human life!

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.440
I see, I see.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:42.740
Marie, here.

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:43.300
Yes.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:45.610
It's just a fever.

00:14:47.480 --> 00:14:51.350
As you can see, I can't go to the mountain.

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:53.950
And I can't afford to be separated from Marie either.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.290
So you'll have to return with the medicine yourself.

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.280
Yes.

00:14:59.290 --> 00:15:00.850
Well, and...

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:02.120
What's the matter?

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:04.630
I don't know if it's because of the fever...

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:08.260
but there's some sort of pattern around his chest and stomach area.

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:11.070
I wonder if it's a parasite. Draw it for me.

00:15:12.670 --> 00:15:14.400
It's not a parasite.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.870
But, I saw this once before.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:23.020
Well, the medicine should reduce the fever for now.

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:25.790
But if he's still not feeling well, bring him here.

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:26.840
Yes.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.490
All right then, here's the medicine and take this as well.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.690
But you already gave me an umbrella.

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:42.500
Don't worry about it. Just hurry up and get back to him.

00:15:43.340 --> 00:15:44.700
Thank you so much.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:46.660
Be careful on the way back!

00:15:46.970 --> 00:15:47.940
Yes!

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:11.750
Elena!

00:16:43.200 --> 00:16:44.660
That's...

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:50.690
Don't worry, Wendy.

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:54.230
We'll get Michael back. You can count on it.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.400
I want my brother's gun.

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:58.280
But...

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:02.480
I want to have it, since it's the only thing he left behind.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:07.490
Hold on, big brother!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.720
That's Van's!

00:17:41.720 --> 00:17:42.750
I...

00:17:42.990 --> 00:17:46.520
I have to help him! That's why!

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:30.730
Van!

00:18:35.110 --> 00:18:36.100
Van?

00:18:38.710 --> 00:18:39.840
Van!

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:46.780
Why?

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:49.420
What's this?

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:52.360
Only the stupid kid's here!

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:54.220
Where's the guy from yesterday?

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:55.930
What's the matter, Zakota?

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:57.260
The guy's not here!

00:18:57.260 --> 00:19:04.610
We spend the whole day searching around and we end up with this?

00:19:04.610 --> 00:19:07.730
Hey, you stupid kid, I'm asking you where he is!

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:11.150
What's the matter? Did he leave you behind?

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:13.450
No! He didn't leave me.

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:17.610
He must be fed up babysitting a stupid kid like you.

00:19:18.390 --> 00:19:20.350
Or are you supposed to be our compensation?

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:26.590
What the hell was that? I thought you were our compensation!

00:19:27.230 --> 00:19:28.960
What's the matter, Zakota?

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:30.000
- Why don't I help you?

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:30.520
- Shut up!
- Why don't I help you?

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:33.300
Who does this stupid kid think she is?

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:38.840
No one from town is coming here. No one will ever find out what we did.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:41.140
Isn't that right, huh?

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:43.200
Van!

00:19:58.860 --> 00:19:59.830
Chesuto!

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:39.360
Where did you go?

00:20:39.600 --> 00:20:42.690
I went through all that trouble trying to take care of you.

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:47.270
You got better all by yourself.

00:20:51.810 --> 00:20:54.010
But, I'm so happy.

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:56.340
Hey...

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:13.060
Go to sleep, you.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:14.600
My name is Wendy.

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:20.030
Hey.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:23.730
I told you to leave me alone.

00:21:26.080 --> 00:21:28.640
Go to sleep. You're a real pain.

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:35.180
Wendy...

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:38.820
Good night.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:46.230
Good night, Van.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:52.170
Well I guess that's it for today, Doc.

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:53.130
Yeah.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:58.940
Yes, hold on a second.

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:02.270
If I'm not mistaken, this patient...

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:07.790
There must be something between him and the man with the artificial arm.

00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:10.820
You're here for a medical exam?

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:14.020
There's something I want to ask.

00:22:14.860 --> 00:22:15.420
Yes.

00:22:16.660 --> 00:22:17.760
What is it?

00:22:20.430 --> 00:22:21.990
I'm looking for...

00:22:23.140 --> 00:22:24.540
a man with a claw.

00:23:53.390 --> 00:23:54.700
Twin's Guards

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:56.830
The place was a sad town.
Twin's Guards

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:57.430
Twin's Guards

00:23:57.430 --> 00:23:59.600
A sad town that seemed as if it had been abandoned...
Twin's Guards

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:00.870
in the bottom of a valley.
Twin's Guards

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:01.270
Twin's Guards

00:24:01.270 --> 00:24:03.970
It was the town where I found out about Van's sad past...
Twin's Guards

00:24:03.970 --> 00:24:05.510
and the reason for his journey.
Twin's Guards

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:06.110
Twin's Guards

00:24:06.110 --> 00:24:08.180
It was all because of Ray.
Twin's Guards

00:24:08.180 --> 00:24:08.810
Twin's Guards

00:24:08.810 --> 00:24:12.710
Even though Ray and Van have very different looks and personalities...
Twin's Guards

00:24:12.710 --> 00:24:15.150
I felt there was something similar about them from the start.
Twin's Guards

00:24:15.150 --> 00:24:15.850
Twin's Guards

00:24:15.850 --> 00:24:18.550
From the time they first met...
Twin's Guards

00:24:18.550 --> 00:24:19.380
Twin's Guards
